# PHASE 2 – REQUIREMENT ANALYSIS

## 1. Introduction

Requirement Analysis is the second phase of the project. In this phase, the requirements needed to develop the Employee Data Import and Management System are identified and analyzed.

The requirements describe what the system should do, what data is required, and what software and hardware are needed.

## 2. Functional Requirements

The system should provide the following functions:

1. Create an employee data table.
2. Import employee data from an Excel spreadsheet.
3. Read employee information from the spreadsheet.
4. Map source fields to target fields.
5. Transform imported data.
6. Create employee records.
7. Display employee records.
8. Update employee information.
9. Delete employee records when required.
10. Validate imported records.
11. Test the imported data.
12. Display the final employee information.

## 3. Non-Functional Requirements

The system should satisfy the following requirements:

* Easy to use
* Reliable
* Accurate
* Maintainable
* Secure
* Fast data processing
* Easy to test
* Easy to understand

## 4. Data Requirements

The project requires the following employee information:

| Field         | Description                  |
| ------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Employee ID   | Unique identification number |
| Employee Name | Name of employee             |
| Department    | Employee department          |
| Email         | Employee email address       |
| Location      | Employee work location       |

## 5. Software Requirements

* ServiceNow Developer Instance
* Web Browser
* Microsoft Excel / Spreadsheet
* Internet Connection
* GitHub

## 6. Hardware Requirements

* Computer or Laptop
* Keyboard
* Mouse
* Internet connection

## 7. User Requirements

The user should be able to:

* Import employee data.
* View employee records.
* Check imported information.
* Identify incorrect data.
* Manage employee records.
* Verify the final result.

## 8. Input Requirements

The system receives employee information through an Excel spreadsheet.

Example:

| Employee ID | Employee Name | Department | Email                                         | Location   |
| ----------- | ------------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------- | ---------- |
| SB-0001     | Arun Kumar    | IT         | [arun@example.com](mailto:arun@example.com)   | Chennai    |
